WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:06.350
Summer blockbuster season is here, and new
trailers are being released nearly every day.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:11.940
It's hard to keep up with the constant influx
of epic footage, so we've compiled a handy

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:17.099
list—here's a rundown of all the trailers
released in May that will absolutely blow

00:00:17.099 --> 00:00:20.529
you away this summer... and beyond...

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:21.710
Okja

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:27.979
Snowpiercer director Bong Joon Ho partnered
with Netflix for Okja, a movie with an all-star

00:00:27.979 --> 00:00:31.849
cast and a deep message about environmental
protection.

00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:36.050
The studio finally released a full trailer
earlier this month, showing off the movie's

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:41.650
gorgeous visuals and its absolutely bizarre
plot: a young girl attempting to rescue her

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:48.010
pet super-pig named Okja before an evil corporation
can turn it into food.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:54.420
Jake Gyllenhaal, Paul Dano, Tilda Swinton,
and Giancarlo Esposito also show up in the

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.310
trailer, which promises a unique thrill ride
from start to finish.

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:00.670
Check it out on June 28.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:01.680
The House

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.890
Starring Will Ferrell and Amy Poehler as two
parents who open up an underground casino

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:12.090
to fill up their daughter's college fund,
The House makes an early bid for the summer's

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.619
raunchiest comedy.

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:18.170
And if the film's Red Band trailer is any
indication, their quick-money scheme doesn't

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:20.460
go as smoothly as they hoped.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.340
Look for all the high-octane hijinks on June
30.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:25.749
Spider-Man: Homecoming

00:01:25.749 --> 00:01:30.619
The final trailer for Spider-Man: Homecoming
really sets this reboot apart from the previous

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:31.740
Spidey films.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:36.119
We get more glimpses of the cool tech that
Tony Stark built into Peter's suit, including

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:37.509
his own version of JARVIS.

00:01:37.509 --> 00:01:41.060
"You have 576 possible web-shooter combinations."

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:45.840
Like past trailers, this footage highlights
how much Tony wants Peter to quit crimefighting,

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.070
but it also offers some fun glimpses of Tony
as a mentor.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:55.280
This dynamic will prove crucial once Spidey
gets started—Michael Keaton's Vulture is

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:00.159
a terrifying villain for young Parker to start
off against, so he'll probably need a lot

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:01.709
of help from Iron Man.

00:02:01.709 --> 00:02:06.659
Finally, it gives us our best look yet at
Donald Glover's mysterious character.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.119
Swing in to see it on July 7.

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:11.590
War For the Planet of the Apes

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:16.110
The final trailer for War for the Planet of
the Apes proves the movie isn't pulling any

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:19.670
punches in the escalating war between man
and ape.

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:24.920
There's a heavy emphasis on the differences
between Andy Serkis' Caesar and Woody Harrelson's

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.510
ruthless Colonel, setting up the humans as
savages, rather than the apes.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:34.820
The trailer also also features a heavy dose
of Steve Zahn's Bad Ape, a new character who

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:37.440
seems destined to become a fan favorite.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:43.720
The trailer promises no mercy and no peace—and
an epic, violent showdown to take the franchise

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.760
to the next level on July 14.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.300
The Big Sick

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.080
This isn't your typical rom-com.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:55.380
The Big Sick stars Silicon Valley's Kumail
Nanjiani, who co-wrote the script alongside

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:00.250
his wife, Emily V. Gordon, based on the true
story of how they met and fell in love.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:05.770
But their biggest problem is one most couples
never have to experience: shortly into their

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:08.320
courtship, Emily falls into a coma.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:13.330
It's a rollercoaster of emotions, and the
movie's early reviews suggest Nanjiani and

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:16.260
Gordon hit them in all the right places.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:20.100
The Big Sick has a June 23rd release date

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.150
Dunkirk

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:26.730
Christopher Nolan is a master of suspense,
and he's proved it again with the second trailer

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:32.980
for his upcoming war thriller Dunkirk, starring
Tom Hardy, Cillian Murphy, Kenneth Branagh,

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:38.850
and former One Direction singer Harry Styles
in the story of the 1940 evacuation of the

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:44.380
French city of Dunkirk, where thousands of
soldiers were left stranded on a beach surrounded

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:45.990
by enemy forces.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:50.850
The trailer definitely gets viewers' pulses
pounding, successfully ramping up anticipation

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:56.040
for an intense, fast-paced experience unlike
any war film you've seen before.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.540
Check it out July 21st.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:03:59.850
Valerian

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:04.350
The final trailer for the upcoming sci-fi
thriller Valerian and the City of a Thousand

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:09.570
Planets doesn't give away much of the plot,
instead focusing on the film's incredible

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:14.270
visuals, teasing a feast for the eyes when
the movie hits the big screen on July 21.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:17.650
Valerian won't just be all visual thrills,
though.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:22.250
Based on a French graphic novel—which also
heavily influenced the visuals of director

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:27.630
Luc Besson's The Fifth Element—Valerian
tells a hell of a story, following two time-traveling

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:33.460
agents tasked with saving the planet Alpha
from a mysterious, all-consuming threat.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:38.650
Clive Owen, John Goodman, Ethan Hawke, and
Rihanna also pop up in the project, which

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:44.500
promises to be another hit sci-fi action film
for the Fifth Element director.

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:46.340
The Dark Tower

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:52.120
Inspired by Stephen King's bestselling saga
of the same name, this adaptation's been many,

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:57.540
many years in the making, but the first trailer
suggests that time might have been just what

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.190
filmmakers needed to get the story right.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:04.940
The trailer is almost all action from start
to finish, starting with an intense dream

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:10.820
experienced by young Jake Chambers—one which
foreshadows a journey into a visually stunning

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:16.070
world grounded by impressive performances
by Idris Elba and Matthew McConaughey.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:20.720
The Dark Tower's trailer doesn't give much
away—instead offering just enough to leave

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:25.440
viewers champing at the bit for the film's
release on August 4.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:26.530
Wind River

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:31.580
Avengers stars Jeremy Renner and Elizabeth
Olsen play very different kinds of heroes

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:36.960
in the upcoming thriller Wind River when they're
tasked with hunting down a killer in the icy

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:39.940
wilderness of the Wind River Indian Reservation.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:46.690
We're ready for a thrilling, intense ride
when Wind River arrives on August 4.

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:48.130
Good Time

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:53.980
From A24, the indie studio behind Get Out,
Good Time stars Robert Pattinson as Connie,

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:59.460
a man on a mission to get his mentally handicapped
brother Nick out of jail after their attempted

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.300
bank robbery goes awry.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:07.130
Pattinson is electric in the trailer, and
early reviews are calling this his best performance

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:13.790
yet in what looks to be one of the most intense—and
beautiful—thrillers released in recent years.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:17.090
Good Time hits studios August 11.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:18.840
The Hitman's Bodyguard

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:23.341
The first trailer for The Hitman's Bodyguard
gave us a lot of action and swearing, but

00:06:23.341 --> 00:06:28.720
the newest preview goes deeper into the film's
story and gives us a glimpse of Gary Oldman

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:30.480
as the ruthless villain.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:35.150
It also teases more of the bickering partnership
between Ryan Reynolds' and Samuel L. Jackson's

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.150
characters.

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:37.150
"27 times.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:39.639
That's how many times he tried to kill me
28!"

00:06:39.639 --> 00:06:45.360
Putting these two together promises the potential
for one of the summer's most explosive comedies.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.550
Look for it August 18.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.090
Logan Lucky

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:54.290
Helmed by acclaimed writer-director Steven
Soderbergh, Logan Lucky is an action-comedy

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:59.960
starring Channing Tatum and Adam Driver as
brothers who decide to rob the Coca-Cola 600,

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:05.710
one of the biggest races of the year...with
the help of inmate Joe Bang, played with gusto

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:07.480
by Daniel Craig.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:11.699
"I am in-car-cer-ate-ed."

00:07:11.699 --> 00:07:17.500
This fun, '80s-inspired trailer uses bright
images, an upbeat score, and a lot of one-liners

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:22.550
to convince viewers to race out to the theater
on August 18.

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:24.550
It Stains the Sand Red

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:30.020
Horror thriller It Stains the Sand Red follows
a woman stuck in the desert pursued by an

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:35.520
untiring member of the undead, and the trailer
promises a picture that flips the genre on

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:39.820
its head and make tired tropes actually scary
again.

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:44.240
Leave the lights on when you check out the
trailer, and prepare to be left on the edge

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:50.210
of your seat waiting for this indie thriller
to scare its way into theaters this summer.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:51.210
It

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:57.290
If you're scared of clowns, the second trailer
for Stephen King's It is definitely not for

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:58.290
you.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:04.010
The terror ramps up quickly with a tiny, horrifying
glimpse of Pennywise the clown.

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:08.840
Bill Skarsgård plays Pennywise, and he's
scaring an impressive cast of experienced

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:14.880
child actors, including St. Vincent's Jaeden
Lieberher and Stranger Things' Finn Wolfhard.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:21.580
As the trailer shows, It isn't short on suspense
or all-out scares, and seems like a safe bet

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:26.630
to be the horror hit of the fall when it hits
theaters on September 8.

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:28.009
Woodshock

00:08:28.009 --> 00:08:32.979
Another potential hit from the studio behind
Get Out, Woodshock stars Kirsten Dunst as

00:08:32.979 --> 00:08:36.270
a woman who tries a drug that triggers hallucinations.

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:41.860
The trailer uses haunting music to show the
inner workings of Dunst's character, who appears

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:43.610
to be hiding a dark secret.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:49.860
This trippy clip opens on a typically dramatic
note but quickly moves into the insane, getting

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:52.110
stranger as it goes on.

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:55.270
Get ready for a trip on September 15.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:57.610
Blade Runner 2049

00:08:57.610 --> 00:09:02.800
If you've been nervous about the upcoming
Blade Runner sequel, this trailer should calm

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:03.800
your fears.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:09.240
The trailer offers a glimpse of a world entrenched
in the culture of the first film, and the

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:14.050
results are so gorgeous and action-packed
that it's impossible to look away.

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:19.130
Even more impressive: it does all this without
giving away too much of the movie's plot.

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:23.270
So feast your eyes, and don't worry about
the spoilers.

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:28.150
Chances are we'll get quite a few surprises
when the film finally arrives on October 6.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.150
Thanks for watching!

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:32.450
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:35.300
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

